    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d67-a2">

                <pb facs="0216" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg98"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 827.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to the Tsung-li Yamên.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-02-25"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 25,
                        1889</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Highness and Your Excellencies</hi>: I have the
                    honor to acknowledge the receipt of the communication of your highness and your
                    excellencies wherein you announce the approaching marriage of His Imperial
                    Majesty the Emperor of China.</p>
                <p>I am directed by the President of the United States to convey to His Imperial
                    Majesty his earnest felicitations on this auspicious event, and to express his
                    sincere hope that these gracious nuptials will be blessed by Heaven, and that
                    happiness and prosperity will always attend their Imperial Majesties.</p>
                <p>Availing myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
